2026-11-03 17:27 Decisions (mine, verksted-worker):
- Root: with plugin setting `workspaces` registered, the folder must lie inside one (`not_in_workspace` otherwise); the OUTERMOST containing registration is the root, so a deeper registration can never skip an ancestor's file; the walk starts there (arch §2). Without registration (my addition beyond §2): every ancestor up to the filesystem root is read and the topmost file is the root. Confinement needs registration: unregistered, a folder outside every configured tree (also via a link/junction out of one) has only the plugin ceiling over it. Registered folders that are missing are skipped; malformed settings refuse every run (`bad_settings`). Walk bound: 64 folders (`folder_too_deep`). The folder is canonical (k6) before the walk, so links resolve first.
- Plugin settings: `workspaces`, `allowed_profiles`, `toolset_ceiling` (plugin.yaml config_schema, type list → Desktop Settings → Plugins JSON editor), read with ctx.get_config = plugins.entries.verksted.settings.<key> of the CALLING profile's config.yaml, frozen into the run. Exercised at ad2b705 in tests/agent/test_hermes_contract.py.
- Merge: missing values inherit; nearest explicit list is the selection; plugin ceiling + every ancestor list are ceilings; a list beyond any earlier ceiling is refused `toolsets_widen`, never clipped; [] is empty; D1(a): under any ceiling an explicit list is required (`toolsets_required`), the ceiling is never sent as the selection. `verksted` is a reserved toolset name in files and ceiling.
- File: only version/profile/toolsets; api_key, base_url, provider, model, env, mcp_servers refused by name; anything else unknown refused; explicit null refused; version must be the int 1 (true/"1"/1.0 refused); profile must match Hermes' PROFILE_ID_RE; 64 KiB cap; UTF-8 (BOM ok); duplicate keys refused; a file that exists but cannot be read fails closed (`bad_config`).
- Profile: nearest wins; another than the parent's must be in allowed_profiles (`profile_not_allowed`) and exist (`profile_missing`, hermes_constants get_default_hermes_root + named_profile_is_live). Switching implemented: Desktop uses host.profileRoutes() route of that profile on the SAME connection (arch §5), plugin API checks the route's profile_id against the frozen session-profile home; store, binding and doorbell stay with the parent (§4). No such route → refused `profile_route_missing` before Hermes is touched. A switched run does NOT tolerate Verksted's own toolset in the child (the depth-1 recursion guard only sees the parent store) → `toolsets_exceeded`; the API flag `own_toolset_tolerated` is read fail-closed.
- Freeze/fingerprint: resolved state incl. file paths + sha256 and ceilings stored at run; status shows it under `config` and `profile`; the Desktop row shows profile ("research (aus default)") and toolsets · Arbeitsbereich · fingerprint.
